WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.180
Open weights just crowned a new leader as Xiaomi's MIMO V2.6 Pro 1T-A42B takes the top spot after training for $3 million. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 181. Xiaomi released the MIMO V2.6 Pro 1T-A42B as the new leading open weights model. The model was trained for $3 million. It crowns Xiaomi as a new Chinese frontier lab in the open weight space.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:34.240
The release shifts attention to cost-efficient training runs that still reach frontier

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:34.960
performance.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:41.300
Builders working with open models should test MIMO V2.6 Pro against current leaders on

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.460
their specific tasks.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:47.420
Watch for follow-up benchmarks on reasoning and agent benchmarks in the coming weeks.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.480
Alibaba unveiled a new powerful chip.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.720
The company also outlined ambitious plans for future AI models.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:00.780
The announcement positions Ali Baba as a stronger domestic player in both hardware and software.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.040
Two separate wire reports covered the same unveiling on the same day.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:09.780
The chip and model plans were presented together as a single coordinated move.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.460
Open AI is working with an independent advisory group of mathematicians.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.900
The group will advise on assessing and communicating new mathematical results.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:24.000
It will also help uphold academic standards and build tools for mathematical research

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.600
research and learning. Mathematicians will shape how AI supports mathematical

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:33.500
and understanding. The advisory group is positioned at the center of how open AI

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:38.600
shares advances in AI and mathematics. Simon Willis in published notes on

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:43.860
Jev. The model represents a new category of system one decision models. These

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:48.680
models focus on judging and deciding rather than chatting. The notes highlight a

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:53.700
shift away from conversational interfaces toward direct decision outputs. Willis

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.560
This in frames Jev as an example of under-invested low-latency intelligence regimes.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:03.640
Andre Carpathi described a point on the LLM Pareto Optimal Curve.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:09.620
The regime features large revealed latent demand for no-thinking, single-token, low-latency

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:10.160
intelligence.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:14.780
This area had been under-invested due to the race toward higher intelligence.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:20.080
Carpathi sees current models as occupying one specific location on that curve.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.780
the observation points to demand that was previously overlooked in favor of

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:30.680
scaling intelligence. Amazon blocked Meta's Muse AI agent. The action targeted

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:35.500
unauthorized agentic shopping behavior. The move highlights growing platform

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:40.400
controls on autonomous agents. The block was issued after the agent performed

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.160
shopping actions without authorization. This is the first public enforcement

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:51.940
action of its kind against a major labs agent. Cardano integrated the X-402 protocol.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:59.420
The integration enables ADA payments directly to AI agents. It expands payment options for autonomous

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:07.140
agent ecosystems. The move allows agents to transact in ADA without intermediaries. Crypto News reported

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:12.020
the integration as a direct bridge between the Cardano blockchain and agent payment flows.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:18.720
NGD launched Whisper Dark. The dungeon crawler game features an AI agent that spends real

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:24.680
ex-gas currency. The project demonstrates practical agent expending in a gaming environment.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:29.260
The agent operates inside the game economy using actual token value.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:35.320
Neo News today covered the launch as an example of agents interacting with real economic systems.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:41.580
Fireflies.ai described how it balances autonomous voice agents with enterprise privacy.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:45.160
The approach separates delegation from judgment tasks.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:49.440
It addresses privacy concerns in enterprise voice agent deployments.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:54.740
The company outlined distinct handling for tasks that require human oversight versus

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:55.680
full economy.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:01.060
The framework was presented as a practical response to enterprise data handling requirements.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:06.880
The SJR architecture decouples multimodal understanding from policy classification.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:11.980
A content model produces structured summaries while a policy model classifies them.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:19.620
The approach achieved a 23.6% relative gain in non-misleading F1 on misleading advertisement detection.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:25.700
A zero-real violation variant matched full data performance within 0.2%.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:31.820
The system was tested on a misleading advertisement detection task with both full and synthetic data.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:42.220
Recipe DB2 compiles 128,942 recipes, with 35,474 ingredients from 32 regions.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:46.160
Ingredient phrases are parsed into seven culinary attributes.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:52.560
Ingredients linked to USDA tables yielding 148 nutritional parameters per mapped item.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.460
The framework makes recipes computable for culinary and nutritional analysis.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:03.840
A random forest classifier propagates 34 ingredient categories across the full vocabulary.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:10.040
Deep Instructor builds an experience graph from 58,607 peer reviews.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:15.440
A React-based agent retrieves dimension-specific evidence for idea evaluation.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:26.140
The system improved Hitat 1 alignment with human judgments by 24.4% and Hitat 2 by 29.7% on the deep instruct data set.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:33.320
The framework was evaluated on controlled, pairwise comparisons across novelty, significance and feasibility.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:38.420
It constructs structured representations from peer-review data to ground evaluations.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:43.600
Treespark reads parent-conditioned distributions from the drafter's Markov head.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:49.420
It calibrates edge acceptance estimates and uses path survival for expansion and stopping.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:57.660
Adaptive trees accept 15-25% more draft tokens per round, and decode 8-14% faster than

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.460
tuned chains.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:02.120
The method gracefully shrinks trees under rising load.

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:06.920
Sampling siblings without replacement keeps decoding lossless at any temperature.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:10.220
factor. Context poisoning occurs when irrelevant or

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.480
confusible tokens raise the maximum attention score among

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:16.460
distractors faster than the evidence margin can keep up.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:22.220
The mechanism follows from softmax retrieval where the decisive evidence score stays bounded

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:25.020
while distractor scores grow with their count.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:31.080
Maintaining fixed accuracy therefore requires the evidence margin to scale as the square root

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.400
of the log of the effective distractor count.

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:39.320
Experiments confirm retrieval accuracy drops as total context grows when hard negatives

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:40.020
are embedded.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:45.860
The same format distractor condition produces the largest accuracy drop at fixed length.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:51.060
Retrieval gating can recover some evidence use, but only when evidence recall itself

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:52.000
is preserved.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:57.800
Teams facing long-context degradation should first measure their actual distractor count,

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:03.140
rather than raw token length, and consider retrieve then-reason pipelines when the margin

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:11.760
cannot scale. Test MIMO V2.6 Pro 1T-A42B on your current open weights benchmarks to see where the

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:18.800
$3 million training run lands relative to prior leaders. Try the SJR moderation pipeline on your

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:24.660
own multimodal policy tasks if you need to bootstrap new policies without real violation examples.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:31.160
Experiment with tree sparks speculative decoding on your inference setup to measure the 8-14%

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.240
wall clock gains under varying load.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:37.820
Explore recipe DB2 for any culinary or nutritional analysis

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:40.860
projects that need structured ingredient and region data.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.900
More open weights releases from Chinese labs

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:47.000
are expected following the Xiaomi and Alibaba announcements.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:50.180
Additional agent payment integrations are likely

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:53.480
as Cardano's X402 work gains traction.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:57.120
Further papers on long context attention interference

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.880
are anticipated given the recent archive activity.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:04.740
Pop the hood on context poisoning and the picture changes from simple length limits

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:07.360
to a precise scaling law on evidence margins.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:13.040
The core issue is that the decisive evidence token keeps a fixed attention score, while

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:16.080
every new distractor can push the maximum score higher.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:21.260
Under the softmax, this forces the required evidence margin to grow with the square root

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:23.020
of the log of the distractor count.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:28.580
Tests showed the biggest accuracy drop when distractors matched the exact format of the

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:34.780
real evidence at fixed context length. Retrieval gating recovers some performance, but only when

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:40.580
the original evidence recall is not itself damaged by the gate. Measure the real distractor count

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:46.340
in your workload first, and switch to retrieve then-reason pipelines once that count exceeds the

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:52.720
margin your model can sustain. Before we go, papers on long context attention interference are

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:58.400
expected to continue appearing. That's models and agents for today. If you found this useful,

